# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRET CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Copy this file:  cp application-secrets.properties.example application-secrets.properties
# 2. Fill in your own values below.
# 3. NEVER commit application-secrets.properties — it is listed in .gitignore.
#
# In production (AWS Elastic Beanstalk) set JWT_SECRET as an environment
# variable in the EB console. The prod profile reads ${JWT_SECRET} with no
# fallback, so the app will refuse to start if the variable is absent.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Minimum 64 random alphanumeric characters.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 64 | tr -d '\n'
jwt-secret=replace-this-with-at-least-64-random-characters-do-not-use-in-production
